---
import ReferenceLayout from "../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro";
---

<ReferenceLayout
	title="Kinra design"
	description="The framework-light design system for Kinra web products and public surfaces."
	current="Overview"
>
	<header class="catalog-header">
		<div class="catalog-header__inner kin-frame">
			<h1 class="kin-title">Kinra design</h1>
			<div>
				<p class="catalog-header__summary">
					A shared visual language for Kinra. Precise tools, thoughtful writing,
					and room for each product to have its own character.
				</p>
				<div class="kin-cluster catalog-header__actions" data-space="compact">
					<a class="kin-button kin-button--primary" href="/examples/"
						>See it in use <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
					>
					<a class="kin-button kin-button--quiet" href="/foundations/"
						>Explore foundations</a
					>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="range-strip" aria-label="Range of the system">
		<div data-kin-scheme="dark">
			<p class="kin-eyebrow">Graphite</p>
			<h2 class="kin-headline">Working surfaces and tools.</h2>
			<p class="kin-body" data-size="sm">
				Quiet structure, cyan signal, mono voice. The default.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div data-kin-scheme="light" data-kin-voice="serif">
			<p class="kin-eyebrow">Paper, serif</p>
			<h2 class="kin-headline">Essays, releases, and considered writing.</h2>
			<p class="kin-body" data-size="sm">
				The same roles on paper, with a serif display voice.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div data-kin-scheme="dark" data-kin-voice="sans">
			<p class="kin-eyebrow" data-tone="reason">Graphite, sans</p>
			<h2 class="kin-headline">Dense application chrome.</h2>
			<p class="kin-body" data-size="sm">
				A sans voice for chrome where mono headings would compete with data.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="layers-heading">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="layers-heading">A layered contract</h2>
			<p>
				Use the smallest stable layer that solves the repeated responsibility.
				Move higher-level code into the owning product.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="kin-grid" data-rules="deep" style="--kin-grid-min: 12rem">
			<article class="layer-card">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
					<rect
						x="4"
						y="4"
						width="16"
						height="16"
						fill="none"
						stroke="currentColor"></rect>
					<rect x="9" y="9" width="6" height="6" fill="currentColor"></rect>
				</svg>
				<h2>Foundations</h2>
				<p>
					Roles for colour, scheme, voice, space, motion, depth, and access.
				</p>
				<a href="/foundations/">Inspect tokens</a>
			</article>
			<article class="layer-card">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
					<path d="M3 5h18M3 12h12M3 19h18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
					></path>
				</svg>
				<h2>Compositions</h2>
				<p>
					Responsive relationships that organize content without styling it.
				</p>
				<a href="/compositions/">Arrange content</a>
			</article>
			<article class="layer-card">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
					<rect
						x="3"
						y="4"
						width="18"
						height="16"
						fill="none"
						stroke="currentColor"></rect>
					<path d="M3 9h18M9 9v11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"></path>
				</svg>
				<h2>Components</h2>
				<p>
					Controls, wayfinding, feedback, evidence, and layers with stable
					contracts.
				</p>
				<a href="/components/">Review components</a>
			</article>
			<article class="layer-card">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
					<path
						d="M4 4h7v7H4zM13 4h7v4h-7zM13 10h7v10h-7zM4 13h7v7H4z"
						fill="none"
						stroke="currentColor"></path>
				</svg>
				<h2>Patterns</h2>
				<p>
					Real product compositions distributed as source to copy and adapt.
				</p>
				<a href="/patterns/">Browse registry</a>
			</article>
			<article class="layer-card">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
					<path
						d="M4 6h16M6 10h12M8 14h8M10 18h4"
						fill="none"
						stroke="currentColor"></path>
				</svg>
				<h2>Surface recipes</h2>
				<p>
					Role adjustments for editorial, docs, learning, operations, and
					application work.
				</p>
				<a href="/surfaces/">Compare jobs</a>
			</article>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="contract-strip" aria-label="Ownership contract">
		<div>
			<p class="kin-eyebrow">Shared and versioned</p>
			<h2>Responsibilities that must not drift</h2>
			<p>
				Tokens, accessible control behavior, layout primitives, assets, and
				compatibility promises belong to the package. So does a vocabulary broad
				enough that no product has to reach for the same three components.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div>
			<p class="kin-eyebrow" data-tone="reason">Copied and source-owned</p>
			<h2>Outcomes that should keep their character</h2>
			<p>
				Routes, product workflows, authored copy, and higher-level composition
				stay with the consumer that understands their job.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</ReferenceLayout>
